From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Keep the shared wpa_sm of the partner links for a
 refused link

__check_assoc_ies() runs for a new link STA of a non-AP MLD with
assoc_wpa_sm set to the wpa_sm of the association link. Its out: path
frees the temporary per-link wpa_sm of the link STA, and it also clears
sta->wpa_sm of every partner link entry of the MLD address. Those
entries, the association link STA among them, hold assoc_wpa_sm and not
the freed instance. On success the partner links get assoc_wpa_sm back;
on failure they keep NULL. This has two effects:

- After a Link Reconfiguration Request whose added link the element
  check refuses, the station stays associated with no wpa_sm on its
  other links. A later valid add of the link crashes hostapd with a
  NULL dereference in wpa_auth_set_ml_info(), called from
  hostapd_ml_process_reconf_link().
- In an association where __check_assoc_ies() refuses a partner link,
  the association goes on over the other links with no wpa_sm, so the
  4-way handshake never starts and the station times out.

Upstream commits 0435c06fc270 ("AP MLD: Update partner link wpa_sm
pointers more consistently") and 3c98f62ac942 ("AP MLD: Clear wpa_sm
entries for all STAs more thoroughly") added the partner clears to
remove pointers to the wpa_sm that is freed. That holds only where the
STA owns the shared wpa_sm. Upstream main 741d70dd8e32 has the same
code.

Clear the partner links only where assoc_wpa_sm is NULL. A link STA
frees its own temporary wpa_sm, and on success still sets assoc_wpa_sm
on its partner links.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6277,7 +6277,10 @@ out:
 		struct wpa_state_machine *sm = sta->wpa_sm;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
-		clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
+		/* The partner links of a link STA hold assoc_wpa_sm, not the
+		 * temporary per-link instance freed here. */
+		if (!assoc_wpa_sm)
+			clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
 		clear_wpa_sm_for_all_sta(hapd, sm);
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
@@ -6296,7 +6299,8 @@ out:
 		} else {
 			sta->wpa_sm = NULL;
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
-			clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
+			if (!assoc_wpa_sm)
+				clear_wpa_sm_for_each_partner_link(hapd, sta);
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 		}
 	}
